From c592dfe9637c65eeaff4c9f6fd869f39ad7ae472 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luiz Augusto von Dentz <luiz.von.dentz@intel.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 16:16:32 -0500
Subject: Bluetooth: hci_sync: Hold hdev->lock in hci_schedule_adv_instance_sync()
Git-commit: c592dfe9637c65eeaff4c9f6fd869f39ad7ae472
Patch-mainline: v7.4-rc5
References: git-fixes

The advertising instance returned by hci_find_adv_instance() was
dereferenced without hdev->lock and could be freed concurrently.

Reported-by: Sashiko <sashiko-bot@kernel.org>
Link: https://sashiko.dev/#/bug/linux-616b1f8e-06ec-4634-a907-5eb4e82f66df
Fixes: cba6b758711c ("Bluetooth: hci_sync: Make use of hci_cmd_sync_queue set 2")
Assisted-by: OpenCode:claude-fable-5.2
Signed-off-by: Luiz Augusto von Dentz <luiz.von.dentz@intel.com>
Acked-by: Takashi Iwai <tiwai@suse.de>

---
 net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c b/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c
index 919c15efe91d..9aac6c3e8b29 100644
--- a/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c
@@ -2207,9 +2207,13 @@ int hci_schedule_adv_instance_sync(struct hci_dev *hdev, u8 instance,
 	if (hdev->adv_instance_timeout)
 		return -EBUSY;
 
+	hci_dev_lock(hdev);
+
 	adv = hci_find_adv_instance(hdev, instance);
-	if (!adv)
+	if (!adv) {
+		hci_dev_unlock(hdev);
 		return -ENOENT;
+	}
 
 	/* A zero timeout means unlimited advertising. As long as there is
 	 * only one instance, duration should be ignored. We still set a timeout
@@ -2239,6 +2243,8 @@ int hci_schedule_adv_instance_sync(struct hci_dev *hdev, u8 instance,
 					       secs_to_jiffies(timeout));
 	}
 
+	hci_dev_unlock(hdev);
+
 	/* If we're just re-scheduling the same instance again then do not
 	 * execute any HCI commands. This happens when a single instance is
 	 * being advertised.
-- 
